\title{Tokamak Control & Simulation}
\meta{slug}{simulation}

\p{
  The interactive console above couples 3D cutaway magnet and plasma geometry (discrete vertical #{B_\phi} toroidal-field cages, signed #{\pm I} poloidal-field shaping rings, nested #{D_\alpha} flux surfaces, and 3D helical #{q_{95}} field lines), 2D poloidal equilibrium cross-sections, and closed-loop policy search trajectories on \code{TCV}, alongside stationary Grad–Shafranov equilibria exported from \code{FUSE.jl 1.2.1} (Meneghini et al. [[Men+24]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.05894)) for \code{SPARC}, \code{ARC}, \code{ITER}, and \code{DIII-D}; § 4 below provides the interactive 56-function \code{OxCaml} synthetic benchmark suite and modal Python C-API bridge, and [Overview](index.html) details the \code{ENN} surrogate and multi-region search formulation.
}

\subtree{
  \title{Exported Tokamak Geometries (\code{FUSE.jl})}

  \p{
    For \code{SPARC}, \code{ARC}, \code{ITER}, and \code{DIII-D} (alongside the 25-vertex \code{TCV} vessel and 20 \code{E}/\code{F}/\code{OH} coils), \code{evals/fuse/worker.jl} initializes \code{IMAS.dd()} device models via \code{FUSE.init}, solves Grad–Shafranov equilibria and active coil currents with \code{ActorEquilibrium(:TEQUILA)}, \code{ActorPFdesign}, and \code{ActorPFactive}, and exports vacuum vessel shells, first-wall contours, toroidal-field \code{TF} D-coils, central solenoid \code{CS}/\code{OH} stacks, poloidal-field \code{PF} rings, and last-closed-flux-surface (\code{LCFS}) contours together with #{I_p}, #{B_0}, #{q_{95}}, #{\beta_N}, and #{P_{\mathrm{fus}}}.
  }
}

\subtree{
  \title{TCV Rampdown Policy Search (\code{toka_gym})}

  \p{
    On the open-source EPFL/MIT \code{toka_gym} TCV plasma rampdown benchmark (Wang et al. [[Wan+25]](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-025-63917-3), Theiler et al. [[The+26]](https://doi.org/10.1088/1741-4326/ae6d12)), a four-layer policy #{\pi_\theta : \mathbb{R}^{11} \to [-1, 1]^8} of hidden width #{256} (#{D = 136{,}712} weights) is searched directly on closed-loop trajectories (#{20} steps #{\times\, 4} substeps) over #{10{,}000} sequential rounds across #{n = 10} common-random-number seeds (#{800{,}000} rollouts across #{8} configurations; initial error \code{58.12 ± 31.39}, exact paired initialization drift \code{0.00}). Multi-region surrogate-free \code{TuRBO-zero} (#{R = 10}, sparse coordinate perturbations of expected block size #{d_p = 13{,}671}) produces identical trajectories across all four cross-region sharing topologies (\code{origin-only}, \code{box-contain}, \code{ellipsoid-ball}, \code{nearest-center}), reaching \code{20.33 ± 6.58} by round #{2}, \code{1.42 ± 0.03} (\code{1.4192 ± 0.0306}) at round #{250}, \code{1.38 ± 0.04} at round #{1{,}000}, \code{1.36 ± 0.03} at round #{3{,}000}, and \code{1.31 ± 0.02} (\code{1.3112 ± 0.0157}) at round #{10{,}000}.
  }

  \p{
    Single-region \code{TuRBO-ENN} (#{R = 1}, #{K = 10} Epistemic Nearest Neighbors fitted by leave-one-out log-likelihood with UCB acquisition; [baux.enn](docs.html#baux.enn)) trails #{R = 10} at round #{250} (\code{1.58 ± 0.05} \code{hyperbolic} to \code{1.68 ± 0.08} \code{euclidean}; \code{wasserstein} \code{1.68 ± 0.06}, exact sign-flip #{p_{\mathrm{Holm}} = 0.014}) and steadily closes the gap over #{10{,}000} rounds, reaching \code{1.34 ± 0.03} (\code{1.3409 ± 0.0301}, \code{wasserstein}, paired difference \code{+0.03 ± 0.04}, #{p_{\mathrm{Holm}} = 1.00}; \code{1.35 ± 0.02} \code{euclidean}; \code{1.35 ± 0.03} \code{hyperbolic}; \code{1.37 ± 0.03} \code{conformal}).
  }

